COMMON NETWORKING ABBREVIATIONS

BASIC NETWORKING TERMS

ADDRESSING
IP    Internet Protocol
      Unique address assigned to devices on a network
      Types: IPv4 (32-bit), IPv6 (128-bit)
      Example: 192.168.1.1 / 2001:db8::1

DNS   Domain Name System
      Translates human-readable domain names into IP addresses
      Variables: A, AAAA, CNAME, MX records

DHCP  Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol
      Automatically assigns IP addresses, subnet mask, gateway, and DNS
      Variables: lease time, scope, reservation

MAC   Media Access Control
      Unique hardware address burned into a network interface
      Format: 00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E (48-bit)

ARP   Address Resolution Protocol
      Maps IP addresses to MAC addresses on a local network

NAT   Network Address Translation
      Allows multiple private devices to share one public IP

NETWORK TYPES
LAN   Local Area Network
      Network confined to a small area (home, office)

WAN   Wide Area Network
      Network spanning large geographic areas (internet)

VLAN  Virtual Local Area Network
      Logically segments a physical network into multiple broadcast domains

SSID  Service Set Identifier
      Name broadcast by a Wi-Fi access point

TRANSPORT LAYER
TCP   Transmission Control Protocol
      Connection-oriented, reliable, ordered delivery
      Fundamentals: handshake, acknowledgments, retransmission

UDP   User Datagram Protocol
      Connectionless, faster, no delivery guarantee
      Used for: DNS, streaming, VoIP

APPLICATION LAYER
HTTP  HyperText Transfer Protocol
      Protocol for web page requests and responses
      Default port: 80

HTTPS HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure
      Encrypted version of HTTP using TLS
      Default port: 443

FTP   File Transfer Protocol
      Transfers files between client and server
      Ports: 20 (data), 21 (control)

SMTP  Simple Mail Transfer Protocol
      Sends email from client to mail server
      Default port: 25 / 587

POP3  Post Office Protocol 3
      Downloads email from server to client
      Default port: 110

IMAP  Internet Message Access Protocol
      Accesses and manages email stored on the server
      Default port: 143 / 993

SECURITY & MANAGEMENT
VPN   Virtual Private Network
      Encrypted tunnel over a public network
      Types: site-to-site, remote-access

QoS   Quality of Service
      Prioritizes certain traffic (voice, video) over others

ICMP  Internet Control Message Protocol
      Used for diagnostics (ping, traceroute)
      Types: Echo Request / Reply

TTL   Time To Live
      Hop limit that prevents packets from circulating forever
      Decremented by 1 at each router

MTU   Maximum Transmission Unit
      Largest packet size a network interface can transmit
      Common value: 1500 bytes (Ethernet)

PoE   Power over Ethernet
      Delivers both data and electrical power over a single Ethernet cable
      Standards: 802.3af / 802.3at / 802.3bt
